      "writtenOn": "2021-11-09T22:01:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This may be a bit problematic depending on the ordering that buildStatements are processed, no? I don\u0027t think Bazel provides any guarantees about the ordering of actions sent in aquery.\n\nWhat if the python zipper action is the first action sent?",
      "revId": "79c5a24ae7e8f39e310e35577502718e539cfc8c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1aeee788_eb5693a3",
        "filename": "bazel/aquery.go",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1318142
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-10T22:45:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Python zip file contains all files so that it can be run by Python interpreter directly, so naturally it should be the last one to be created after all other artifacts of py_binary are created. I think Bazel collects all actions in a way that for later execution dependencies are created first, and the order of actions in aquery output should reflect that execution sequence properly. But that might be just my expectation and wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "f4ff16cb_79c203b5",
      "revId": "79c5a24ae7e8f39e310e35577502718e539cfc8c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
