      "writtenOn": "2021-11-10T23:29:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This description of the function semantics is still confusing -- perhaps because it is too focused on describing the reason it exists, and less so what it actually does.\n\nConsider an alternate description of this function:\n\n```\n// addOutputToBuildStatements finds all buildStatements which contain requiredOutput, \n// and for each such buildStatement, adds newInput as an input to that buildStatement.\nfunc addOutputToBuildStatements(buildStatements *[]BuildStatement, requiredOutput string, newInput string) {\n   ...\n}\n```\n\nThen the caller would call `addOutputToBuildStatements(\u0026buildStatements, outputPaths[0] + \".zip\", outputPaths[0])`, instead of addPythonZipFileAsDependencyOfPythonBinary.\n\n\nAs general feedback, the comment that describes a function should describe what the function does. You can follow up with a description for why the function needs to exist only after you have described what the function does.",
      "parentUuid": "dcfaf6ed_012569eb",
